# Your Stream app's public key. Leave it unset to run against Stream's demo
# app. This is the variable name that `getstream env --target vite` writes,
# so you can generate it instead of pasting it by hand. (VITE_API_KEY is
# still read as a fallback.)
# VITE_STREAM_API_KEY=

# Optional. If unset, the app defaults to user_id "react-tutorial" and
# derives user_name from it. You can also override either value per-run
# via URL params:  ?user_id=alice&user_name=Alice
# VITE_USER_ID=react-tutorial
# VITE_USER_NAME=React Tutorial

# A user token for VITE_USER_ID, issued for the app above - the one the
# tutorial has you paste. Used whenever set, unless ?user_id= switches to
# another user.
# VITE_USER_TOKEN=

# Optional. Token endpoint used to mint a fresh JWT for the active user_id
# when no VITE_USER_TOKEN is set. Defaults to Stream's demo endpoint, whose
# tokens only work with the demo app's API key; point it at a token service
# for your own app, or set VITE_USER_TOKEN instead.
# VITE_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://pronto.getstream.io/api/auth/create-token
# VITE_TOKEN_ENVIRONMENT=demo
